WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.851
(delicate haunting music)

00:00:03.851 --> 00:00:06.997
- [Narrator] To wander this
mausoleum in Shiraz, Iran

00:00:06.997 --> 00:00:11.080
is like stepping into the
holiest of light shows.

00:00:15.276 --> 00:00:17.464
The Shah Cheragh which roughly translates

00:00:17.464 --> 00:00:20.166
to king of the light in Persian.

00:00:20.166 --> 00:00:22.433
Is a funerary monument and mosque,

00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:27.383
a beautiful holy place for
thousands of Muslim worshipers.

00:00:27.383 --> 00:00:29.607
The structure is made
of multi-colored pieces

00:00:29.607 --> 00:00:32.265
of tile and glass and is considered to be

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:36.203
the third most important
pilgrimage site in Iran.

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:39.468
Initially started around
900 A.D. as a burial site

00:00:39.468 --> 00:00:42.083
for an important Shia Muslim figure,

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:46.058
the mosque continued to
be expanded and improved.

00:00:46.058 --> 00:00:47.700
The decision to adorn the mosque

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.257
with its iconic mirror ball decoration

00:00:50.257 --> 00:00:54.026
came from Queen Tash
Khatun in the 14th century.

00:00:54.026 --> 00:00:56.288
She wanted the mosque
to intensify any light

00:00:56.288 --> 00:01:00.867
a thousand times over, an
homage to the mosque's name.

00:01:00.867 --> 00:01:02.625
Although meant to be a holy shrine

00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:05.501
and important pilgrimage
location for Shia Muslims,

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:07.445
people of any faith can marvel

00:01:07.445 --> 00:01:10.028
at the mosque's immense beauty.

00:01:12.953 --> 00:01:15.370
(tone rings)

